file=Behavioural Science/bias/operational/principles/bias-principles.md · b·p:bias \· principles=> Universal-only.\n\n1. **Specific bias, specific rationale** — no blanket "confirmation bias risk" without example.\n2. **Counter-exercise is prescriptive**, not "be aware".\n3. **Vulnerable populations = extra scrutiny.**\n4. **Dark patterns = auto-reject.**\n5. **Belmont framework** — respect for persons \· beneficence \· justice.\n6. **Independent generation before discussion** on pre-mortem.\n7. **Rejection routes back for redesign**, not silent kill.\n8. **Attach audits + reviews to decision gate record.**\n9. **Never over-flags** — 8-of-8 high on bias audit means audit is broken.\n10. **Verification-before-completion inherited.**\n